This directory is populated by ../../run.sh, which copies the orchestrator's
real ranking source here before building:

    skills.rs       from crates/thetis/src/
    skill_lint.rs   from crates/thetis/src/   (stubbed if the revision predates it)
    skill_index.rs  from crates/thetis/src/
    table.rs        generated by extract.py from agents/agent-core/src/groups.rs

The copies are gitignored on purpose. Their content depends on which revision is
being measured, so checking them in would freeze the benchmark against whatever
the source looked like on the day it was written -- which is precisely the thing
this design avoids by lifting rather than restating.

Run ./run.sh, not cargo, or the build fails with "file not found for module".
